MlKemKeyPair
-------------
  new()
      Result<Self, CipherboxError>
      ML-KEM-768 key pair.

  new_with_level(level: KemLevel)
      Result<Self, CipherboxError>
      Either ML-KEM-768 or ML-KEM-1024.

  from_seed(seed: &[u8])
      Result<Self, CipherboxError>
      From a 64-byte seed (d || z), ML-KEM-768.

  from_seed_with_level(seed: &[u8], level: KemLevel)
      Result<Self, CipherboxError>
      Either level.

  encapsulate()
      Result<(Vec<u8>, Vec<u8>), CipherboxError>
      Encapsulate to this key pair's own public key.

  decapsulate(ciphertext: &[u8])
      Result<Vec<u8>, CipherboxError>
      Implicit rejection on invalid ciphertext.

  export_keys() -> (Vec<u8>, Vec<u8>)
      (dk_seed_64, ek). The level is recoverable from the ek
      length (1184 or 1568 bytes).

  import_keys(dk_seed: &[u8], ek: &[u8])
      Result<Self, CipherboxError>
      The ek must match the seed, and is checked against the
      level's key-validation routine.

  level() -> KemLevel
  encapsulation_key() -> &[u8]
  decapsulation_key() -> &[u8]

